[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: weft system requirements
VERSION: 0.1 (draft)
OPTIONS:
  MARKUP: Text

[GRAMMAR]
ELEMENTS:
- TAG: SECTION
  PROPERTIES:
    IS_COMPOSITE: True
  FIELDS:
  - TITLE: UID
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: TITLE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
- TAG: TEXT
  FIELDS:
  - TITLE: UID
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: STATEMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
- TAG: REQUIREMENT
  FIELDS:
  - TITLE: UID
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: STATUS
    TYPE: SingleChoice(Draft, Active, Deleted)
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: VERIFICATION
    TYPE: SingleChoice(Test, Analysis, Inspection, Demonstration)
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: TITLE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: STATEMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: DERIVED_FROM
    HUMAN_TITLE: Derived from (principles, docs/04)
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: DOCS
    HUMAN_TITLE: Design docs
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: STANDARDS
    HUMAN_TITLE: Standards (draft mapping)
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: FACTS
    HUMAN_TITLE: Facts (facts.toml)
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  RELATIONS:
  - TYPE: Parent
  - TYPE: File

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
System-level requirements of weft. They are derived from the principles D1-D9 (docs/04) and refine the adoption contract (docs/14 §2), the conflict model (docs/05), topologies (docs/13) and the pub/sub transport contract (docs/15).

Component requirements in other repositories (for example weft-verifier/requirements/) refer to these with a SATISFIES field. `just check` fails when a reference is unknown, or when an Active requirement verified by Test is not satisfied by any component requirement. Draft requirements are designed but not yet implemented.

STANDARDS is a draft mapping to IEC 62443-4-2 and CRA Annex I; it has not been reviewed by an assessor.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Adoption contract

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-001
STATUS: Active
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Authority comes from keys
STATEMENT: >>>
Desired state shall reach a device only as signed weft documents under a tenant trust anchor. No server or path shall be able to command a device into a new state.
<<<
DERIVED_FROM: D3
DOCS: docs/14 §2.1
STANDARDS: IEC 62443-4-2 CR 2.1, CR 3.4; CRA Annex I Part I 2(d), 2(f)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-002
STATUS: Active
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: The device decides
STATEMENT: >>>
Every managed device shall decide locally with weft-verifier, or be managed by a proxy that runs the verifier on its behalf and is shown as such in the inventory.
<<<
DERIVED_FROM: D3, D9
DOCS: docs/14 §2.2, docs/18
STANDARDS: IEC 62443-4-2 CR 2.1

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-003
STATUS: Draft
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Separate, minimal executor
STATEMENT: >>>
A device shall apply only the verifier's instructions, through a small executor separated from transport and decision code.
<<<
DERIVED_FROM: D9
DOCS: docs/07, docs/14 §2.2
STANDARDS: IEC 62443-4-2 CR 2.1; CRA Annex I Part I 2(j)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-004
STATUS: Draft
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Per-device identity
STATEMENT: >>>
Each device shall have its own key pair, hardware-backed where the hardware allows. Device identity is the key, not a name or an address.
<<<
DERIVED_FROM: D3, D6
DOCS: docs/10, docs/14 §2.3
STANDARDS: IEC 62443-4-2 CR 1.2, CR 1.5

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-005
STATUS: Active
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Content-addressed, forward-only components
STATEMENT: >>>
Every deployable thing shall be a named component referring to an artifact by digest, and versions shall only move forward per slot.
<<<
DERIVED_FROM: D3
DOCS: docs/14 §2.4
STANDARDS: IEC 62443-4-2 CR 3.4; CRA Annex I Part I 2(c)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-006
STATUS: Draft
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Persist before acting
STATEMENT: >>>
Decision state (version marks, time floor, revocations) shall be persisted atomically before the device acts on a decision, and shall survive power loss.
<<<
DERIVED_FROM: D2, D3
DOCS: docs/11, docs/14 §2.5
STANDARDS: IEC 62443-4-2 CR 3.4

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-007
STATUS: Active
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Versions order, clocks do not
STATEMENT: >>>
Ordering of documents shall come from versions. Wall time shall only be used as a forward-only lower bound for expiry.
<<<
DERIVED_FROM: D2
DOCS: docs/11, docs/14 §2.6
STANDARDS: IEC 62443-4-2 CR 2.11

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-008
STATUS: Draft
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Reported state in weft terms
STATEMENT: >>>
Devices shall report state, conflicts and withheld components in the weft vocabulary, independent of how the report travels.
<<<
DERIVED_FROM: D3
DOCS: docs/05 §2.3b, docs/14 §2.7
STANDARDS: IEC 62443-4-2 CR 2.8; CRA Annex I Part I 2(l)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-009
STATUS: Draft
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Envelope and topic namespace
STATEMENT: >>>
Messages that use weft pub/sub shall use the weft envelope and topic namespace; the transport is free.
<<<
DERIVED_FROM: D1, D4
DOCS: docs/05 §1, docs/15 §3.4
FACTS: pubsub.topic.segment_max, pubsub.topic.max_depth, pubsub.topic.max_len

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Decisions and conflicts

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-010
STATUS: Active
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Deterministic precedence
STATEMENT: >>>
Precedence between authorized documents shall be a number, with names given by the tenant's scope profile.
<<<
DERIVED_FROM: D3
DOCS: docs/05 §2.3
STANDARDS: IEC 62443-4-2 CR 2.1
FACTS: priority.default.fleet, priority.default.group, priority.default.site, priority.default.device, priority.default.local

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-011
STATUS: Active
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Conflicts are never silent
STATEMENT: >>>
Conflicting changes shall never be resolved by hidden tie-breaking: ties apply neither change, locks are respected, and every conflict is reported with an id that is the same on every device.
<<<
DERIVED_FROM: D3
DOCS: docs/05 §2.3, §2.3b
STANDARDS: IEC 62443-4-2 CR 2.8, CR 3.6

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-012
STATUS: Active
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Rollback and equivocation protection
STATEMENT: >>>
Devices shall reject older versions than they accepted, and shall detect different documents with the same version.
<<<
DERIVED_FROM: D3
DOCS: docs/05, docs/07
STANDARDS: IEC 62443-4-2 CR 3.4; CRA Annex I Part I 2(c), 2(f)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-013
STATUS: Active
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Fail safe when incomplete
STATEMENT: >>>
When information needed for a decision is missing, the device shall keep its current state for that component instead of acting on partial state.
<<<
DERIVED_FROM: D3, D9
DOCS: docs/07
STANDARDS: IEC 62443-4-2 CR 3.6

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-014
STATUS: Active
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Delegation narrows
STATEMENT: >>>
Delegated rights shall never exceed the delegator's rights, and shall be limited in time.
<<<
DERIVED_FROM: D3
DOCS: docs/06
STANDARDS: IEC 62443-4-2 CR 1.9, CR 2.1

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-015
STATUS: Active
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Monotonic revocation
STATEMENT: >>>
Revocation shall be permanent and shall not need coordination.
<<<
DERIVED_FROM: D3
DOCS: docs/04 (CALM), docs/06
STANDARDS: IEC 62443-4-2 CR 1.9

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-016
STATUS: Active
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Strict, bounded input in the trusted path
STATEMENT: >>>
All parsers in the trusted path shall accept exactly one encoding per value and shall bound memory, depth and work for any input, without panicking.
<<<
DERIVED_FROM: D9
DOCS: docs/07
STANDARDS: IEC 62443-4-2 CR 3.5, CR 3.7, CR 7.2; CRA Annex I Part I 2(h), 2(j)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-017
STATUS: Active
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Same inputs, same decision
STATEMENT: >>>
Devices given the same documents shall reach the same decisions, whatever order or path the documents arrived in.
<<<
DERIVED_FROM: D3, D4
DOCS: docs/13 §3
STANDARDS: IEC 62443-4-2 CR 3.6

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Offline and topology

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-020
STATUS: Draft
VERIFICATION: Demonstration
TITLE: Works without cloud
STATEMENT: >>>
Every function (configuration, deployments, updates, conflicts, local UI) shall work with no cloud or internet connection.
<<<
DERIVED_FROM: D2
DOCS: docs/01 P15, docs/13

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-021
STATUS: Active
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Trust independent of path
STATEMENT: >>>
Integrity shall come from end-to-end signatures, so any relay, uplink, bridge or removable medium may carry documents without being trusted.
<<<
DERIVED_FROM: D3, D4
DOCS: docs/13 §3, docs/16
STANDARDS: IEC 62443-4-2 CR 3.4

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-022
STATUS: Draft
VERIFICATION: Demonstration
TITLE: Roles by configuration
STATEMENT: >>>
Node roles (endpoint, relay, uplink, proxy, site services) shall be assigned by signed configuration, with the same build for all topologies.
<<<
DERIVED_FROM: D4
DOCS: docs/13 §1

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Pub/sub transport contract

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-030
STATUS: Draft
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: T1: hierarchical keys
STATEMENT: >>>
A transport shall support publishing to hierarchical keys and subscribing by prefix and single-level wildcard.
<<<
DERIVED_FROM: D1, D4
DOCS: docs/15 §1

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-031
STATUS: Draft
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: T2: binary payloads
STATEMENT: >>>
A transport shall carry opaque binary payloads of at least the minimum size, preferably the preferred size.
<<<
DERIVED_FROM: D1, D4
DOCS: docs/15 §1, §4
FACTS: pubsub.payload_min, pubsub.payload_preferred

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-032
STATUS: Draft
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: T3: best effort is enough
STATEMENT: >>>
weft shall be correct over best-effort transports; loss, duplicates and reordering shall be handled end to end.
<<<
DERIVED_FROM: D1, D4
DOCS: docs/15 §1, §3

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-033
STATUS: Draft
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: T4: link state
STATEMENT: >>>
A transport adapter shall report local link state, which drives store and forward and resynchronisation.
<<<
DERIVED_FROM: D2, D4
DOCS: docs/15 §1

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-034
STATUS: Draft
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: T5: authenticated peers
STATEMENT: >>>
Transport peers and clients shall be authenticated per node identity, for transport access control.
<<<
DERIVED_FROM: D4
DOCS: docs/15 §1, docs/16
STANDARDS: IEC 62443-4-2 CR 1.2

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-035
STATUS: Draft
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: T6: prefix ACLs
STATEMENT: >>>
Transports with a broker or router shall enforce ACLs by key prefix per identity, generated from the weft policy.
<<<
DERIVED_FROM: D4
DOCS: docs/06, docs/15 §1
STANDARDS: IEC 62443-4-2 CR 2.1

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Platform

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-040
STATUS: Active
VERIFICATION: Inspection
TITLE: Permissive licences
STATEMENT: >>>
weft shall be MIT licensed, and its core shall contain no GPLv3, AGPL, BSL or SSPL dependencies.
<<<
DERIVED_FROM: D5
DOCS: docs/03
FACTS: license.weft

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-041
STATUS: Active
VERIFICATION: Inspection
TITLE: Minimal trusted code
STATEMENT: >>>
Security decisions shall live in weft-verifier: no_std, no unsafe code, no I/O.
<<<
DERIVED_FROM: D9
DOCS: docs/07
STANDARDS: CRA Annex I Part I 2(j), 2(k)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-042
STATUS: Active
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Crypto agility
STATEMENT: >>>
Signed data shall carry algorithm identifiers, so that algorithms can be added and retired, including post-quantum ones.
<<<
DERIVED_FROM: D6
DOCS: docs/01 P12, docs/18 §3

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-043
STATUS: Active
VERIFICATION: Inspection
TITLE: Supported targets
STATEMENT: >>>
Trusted-path code shall build for x86-64, arm64 and riscv64 Linux, and for Cortex-M and RISC-V microcontrollers.
<<<
DERIVED_FROM: D8
DOCS: docs/12 §5

[[/SECTION]]
